      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "detail": "the pair machinery asserts every round that the two sides' claims sum to what they summed to before the transfer. A network that quietly loses a thousandth of its holdings each round was planted and the assertion fired. A check nobody has seen fail is not known to work.",
      "kind": "instrument",
      "name": "A40-1  pair-level conservation, and the check that would catch its absence",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "detail": "Void: printed, not adjudicated. This is the description rule 13 puts before any test, and no criterion was registered on which gap should close. Each gap is a log ratio of the leading side to the lagging one, so zero is closed whatever the units. The lagging side starts with 50% of the other's claims and nothing else differs. level: opens +0.551, shut boundary closes to +0.476, widest closes to +0.451, moved 0.025 against a seed floor of 0.002 | support: opens -0.263, shut boundary closes to -0.437, widest closes to -0.412, moved 0.025 against a seed floor of 0.020 | active_nodes: opens +0.000, shut boundary closes to +0.000, widest closes to +0.000, moved 0.000 against a seed floor of 0.000 | layer2_reached: opens +0.000, shut boundary closes to +0.000, widest closes to +0.000, moved 0.000 against a seed floor of 0.000 | layer1_volume: opens +0.837, shut boundary closes to +0.947, widest closes to +0.892, moved 0.055 against a seed floor of 0.008. Floor measured, not declared: the seed spread of the closing figure at a shut boundary, where nothing crossed.",
      "kind": "own_reading",
      "name": "A40-2  which candidate gap the boundary closes",
      "passed": null,
      "void": true
    },
    {
      "detail": "one seed, initial claims over a sixteenfold range (0.125, 0.5, 2.0, 4.0 times the reference). Active nodes and the share of the second layer reached are bitwise identical at every stock: worst absolute difference 0.0000. Over the same range the level is sublinear and the support set moves the other way: x0.125 -> volume x0.18; x0.5 -> volume x0.62; x2 -> volume x1.76; x4 -> volume x3.27 against support x1.93; support x1.55; support x0.76; support x0.65. **So a pure difference in the claim stock is invisible in who takes part, and the level and the support set are two directions rather than one.** That is why two of the candidate gaps in A40-2 read exactly zero: they have no object on this axis, which is a property of the module and not a bug.",
      "kind": "instrument",
      "name": "A40-4  the claim stock does not move who takes part, at all",
      "passed": true
    },
    {
      "detail": "the field-exact arm. A22 forced w = d phi on A3's carrier and read that the whole holonomy carries 1.33% of the support contraction there, the graph carrying the rest. Whether catch-up splits the same way between the two channels is the question this station opens and does not answer: A22's construction sits on a different carrier and joining the two is its own piece of work. Registered here so the next session does not re-derive the need.",
      "kind": "bookkeeping",
